WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.300 --> 00:00:02.133
A vacancy.

2
00:00:02.183 --> 00:00:03.811
A strong shortlist.

3
00:00:03.861 --> 00:00:06.726
Candidates who convince on paper.

4
00:00:06.776 --> 00:00:11.273
But a curriculum vitae mainly tells you what someone has done.

5
00:00:11.323 --> 00:00:16.773
The real question is: who truly fits this role,
this team and this context?

6
00:00:16.823 --> 00:00:21.783
That is what the Recruitment & Role Fit journey makes visible.

7
00:00:21.833 --> 00:00:27.521
It supports a hiring decision that
looks further than experience alone.

8
00:00:27.571 --> 00:00:35.506
The starting point is the congruence between talent,
drivers, energy and the real context of the role.

9
00:00:35.556 --> 00:00:40.751
Not as a separate score,
but as a well-founded comparative picture.

10
00:00:40.801 --> 00:00:54.781
That is how it becomes visible what makes someone naturally strong, what gives or costs energy,
and where the match with role, team and assignment becomes durable, or stays vulnerable.

11
00:00:54.831 --> 00:00:56.652
That sharpens the choice.

12
00:00:56.702 --> 00:01:04.812
Not only who convinces today, but who has the greatest
chance of truly coming into their own in this context.

13
00:01:04.862 --> 00:01:18.094
For recruiters, HR and managers, this creates a fairer and stronger decision,
with concrete points of attention for the interview, the comparison and the onboarding.

14
00:01:18.896 --> 00:01:21.218
No automatic selection.

15
00:01:21.318 --> 00:01:23.910
No replacement for the conversation.

16
00:01:24.010 --> 00:01:25.881
The platform advises.

17
00:01:25.981 --> 00:01:28.241
The organisation decides.

